      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the product of the two numbers given that their least common multiple (LCM) is 36 and their greatest common divisor (GCD) is 6, we can use the relationship between the LCM, GCD, and the product of the two numbers. The relationship is expressed by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) = 36\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{GCD}(a, b) = 6\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nCalculating the product on the left side:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = 216\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of the two numbers is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
